7
00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:34.233
To define. Change.

8
00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:40.799
And I'll abbreviate this one.

9
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.866
Opportunity. Now, to begin let me define an opportunity.

10
00:00:46.866 --> 00:00:51.466
An opportunity is a set of conditions.

11
00:00:51.466 --> 00:00:57.366
That's a key thought there. It's a set of conditions

12
00:00:57.366 --> 00:01:03.199
that's favorable to an end.

13
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:10.133
A set of conditions that is favorable to some end. That's an opportunity.

14
00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:14.366
So, now in the language of Six Sigma. I can say

15
00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:21.132
that an opportunity is a function of the first condition

16
00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:25.133
to the Nth condition.

17
00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:31.666
Now, what do I mean by that? Some of you may recall from other sessions,

18
00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:35.799
where I talked about getting a job.

19
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.600
So, you want a job opportunity.

20
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.733
Well, one condition of an opportunity is you gotta be looking.

21
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:47.999
You gotta have a need for a job.

22
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.833
Another opportunity is that you take the newspaper

23
00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:55.966
to read the potential jobs that are open.

24
00:01:55.966 --> 00:02:00.066
Another condition is that you can read.

25
00:02:00.066 --> 00:02:07.099
See. So, those things have gotta be present for you have a job opportunity. It's that simple.

26
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:14.100
Now, condition one to condition N. What do we mean of that? Well, that's the first condition.

27
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:18.366
See, I could just as easily said this, condition one comma, condition two comma,

28
00:02:18.366 --> 00:02:22.366
condition three comma, dot dot dot, condition N.

29
00:02:22.366 --> 00:02:25.832
Through the Nth condition. Where there is a large number of conditions.

30
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:29.466
Now, we gotta remember this. Hey, this is very important.

31
00:02:29.466 --> 00:02:32.399
Not all these conditions are equally weighted.

32
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.166
Some conditions carry more weight than others,

33
00:02:36.166 --> 00:02:42.066
and that's called the vital few versus the trivial many.

34
00:02:42.066 --> 00:02:49.032
So, what I want to do is go find the vital few conditions that create. Listen to this now.

35
00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:52.499
Keyword I want to go identify.

36
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:58.433
I want to go define the vital few conditions

37
00:02:58.433 --> 00:03:04.399
that creates change opportunity.

38
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:10.366
And what change are we talking about? We’re talking about this change.

39
00:03:10.366 --> 00:03:15.832
To go from the is to the ought condition of each,

40
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:19.833
value need we have, each utility, access, worth need.

41
00:03:19.833 --> 00:03:26.699
So again, I want to define the change opportunity.

42
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:32.066
That's defining the conditions

43
00:03:32.066 --> 00:03:37.799
that has to change, to create the opportunity,

44
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.300
to close the gaps.

45
00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:48.166
Thereby improving the quality of my life. Thereby bringing greater value into my life.

46
00:03:48.166 --> 00:03:52.266
That's what we’re talking about,

47
00:03:52.266 --> 00:03:56.766
when we say define change opportunity.

48
